---
/**
 * /course/ is waitlist only for now (docs/SPEC.md §11).
 *
 * The page is deliberately honest that it is not built yet: a waitlist that
 * pretends to be a product converts once and burns the list. The outline below
 * describes work that genuinely exists: the board engine, the two video
 * styles, and the measured pacing rules, so nothing here is a promise we
 * cannot keep.
 *
 * The page now carries one commercial offer: early access at a founding rate of
 * EUR 39/month, locked for the life of the membership, with limited positions.
 * No payment is taken, so this collects a name and an email and nothing else.
 * The count of places taken is deliberately NOT shown; it goes to the daily
 * Telegram report instead (user, 2026-08-09).
 *
 * TODO(thanos): "who is it for" in one line, then this copy gets tightened.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import NewsletterForm from '../components/NewsletterForm.astro'
import EarlyAccessForm from '../components/EarlyAccessForm.astro'
import { abs } from '../lib/site'

const modules = [
  {
    n: '01',
    title: 'The two styles',
    body: 'The tactics board and the story short are different crafts. One teaches a system with choreography and no narration; the other carries a career or a night through portraits, type and pacing. You build one of each.',
  },
  {
    n: '02',
    title: 'The board engine',
    body: 'A reusable, scale-accurate pitch with tokens, a ball locked to the carrier, a follow-camera, and role cues that reassign themselves as the ball moves. Once this exists, a new breakdown is choreography rather than construction.',
  },
  {
    n: '03',
    title: 'Choreography',
    body: 'Why an eased fast-then-slow move reads as professional and a linear one does not. Holding a beat, staggering reveals so value keeps arriving, and the single most common failure: showing everything in four seconds and then sitting still.',
  },
  {
    n: '04',
    title: 'Sound without a licence',
    body: 'Synthesising your own effect kit, mapping cues tightly to motion, and ducking a bed under the transients. Copyright-safe by construction, which matters more in football than in any other niche.',
  },
  {
    n: '05',
    title: 'What the numbers actually say',
    body: 'The pacing rules in this course are not taste. They came out of measuring 88 published shorts: where attention is lost, which second decides it, and why a whole-team system outperforms a technique clinic by a factor of seven.',
  },
  {
    n: '06',
    title: 'Shipping',
    body: 'Export settings, the safe zones each platform crops, caption placement, and the trim discipline that turned out to matter more than anything done in the render.',
  },
]

const breadcrumb = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [{ '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Course', item: abs('/course/') }],
}
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The course: how these videos get made"
  description="How the Total Football breakdowns are made, end to end. Get early access and lock the founding rate of EUR 39 a month for life. Limited positions."
  path="/course/"
  structuredData={[breadcrumb]}
>
  <section class="stage border-b border-ink-hair">
    <div class="shell py-20 md:py-28">
      <div class="max-w-[46rem]">
        <p class="micro mb-7" data-reveal="fade">In production</p>
        <h1 class="text-display font-black" data-reveal="clip" data-reveal-delay="80">
          How these are<br /><span class="grad-text">actually made.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-9 max-w-prose text-xl leading-[1.6] text-ink/85">
          Not a motion-graphics course with a football example bolted on. The specific pipeline that
          produced this channel: the engine, the choreography, and the pacing rules that came out of
          measuring what people actually watched.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-11 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
          <a href="#early-access" class="btn-primary">Get early access</a>
          <span class="text-[13px] text-ink-soft">
            Lock <strong class="font-bold text-ink">€39/month</strong> for life
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ── Early access ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
      The one commercial offer on the site. It asks for a name as well as an
      email because it is a held place rather than a mailing list, and the
      price promise only means something if we know who it was made to. */}
  <section id="early-access" class="scroll-mt-20 border-b border-ink-hair bg-paper-deep/40">
    <div class="shell py-20 md:py-28">
      <div class="grid gap-14 lg:grid-cols-[0.95fr_1.05fr] lg:items-start">
        <div>
          <p class="micro mb-6" data-reveal="fade">Early access · limited positions</p>
          <h2 class="text-title font-black" data-reveal="clip">
            Lock <span class="grad-text">€39/month</span> for life.
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-6 max-w-prose text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
            The course is still being built. Join now and you hold a place in the first intake at
            €39 a month, and that rate stays yours for as long as you keep your membership, whatever
            the price becomes later.
          </p>

          <ul class="mt-9 space-y-4">
            {
              [
                ['€39 / month, locked', 'The founding rate. It never rises for you, even when it rises for everyone else.'],
                ['Limited positions', 'The first intake is deliberately small so the feedback is real feedback.'],
                ['First through the door', 'You get access the day it opens, before it is announced anywhere.'],
                ['Nothing to pay today', 'No card, no deposit. You are holding a place and a price, not buying yet.'],
              ].map(([title, body], i) => (
                <li class="flex gap-4" data-reveal data-reveal-delay={i * 70}>
                  <span
                    class="mt-1.5 h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-tf-gradient"
                    aria-hidden="true"
                  />
                  <span>
                    <strong class="block text-[15px] font-bold">{title}</strong>
                    <span class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">{body}</span>
                  </span>
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div
          class="rounded-3xl border border-ink-hair bg-surface/60 p-8 shadow-paper md:p-10"
          data-reveal="rise"
        >
          <div class="mb-8 flex items-baseline gap-3">
            <span class="text-5xl font-black tabular-nums">€39</span>
            <span class="text-[15px] font-semibold text-ink-soft">/ month, for life</span>
          </div>
          <div class="rule mb-8"></div>
          <EarlyAccessForm />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shell py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="mb-14 max-w-prose">
      <p class="micro mb-6">The outline</p>
      <h2 class="text-title font-black" data-reveal="clip">Six parts, one finished short at the end.</h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        Subject to change while it is being built, and the waitlist gets told when it does.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-3xl bg-ink-hair md:grid-cols-2">
      {
        modules.map((m, i) => (
          <li class="bg-paper p-8 transition-colors duration-300 hover:bg-surface/70 md:p-10" data-reveal="rise" data-reveal-delay={i * 70}>
            <span class="mb-5 block bg-tf-gradient bg-clip-text text-2xl font-black tabular-nums text-transparent">
              {m.n}
            </span>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-black leading-tight">{m.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">{m.body}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-ink-hair">
    <div class="shell py-20">
      <div class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] md:items-end">
        <div class="max-w-prose">
          <p class="micro mb-5">Not ready to commit?</p>
          <h2 class="text-section font-black">Just get told when it opens.</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
            No launch spam, and no locked price. One email when there is something real to look at.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="w-full max-w-md shrink-0">
          <NewsletterForm source="course-waitlist" cta="Notify me" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
